O|                         
N|          FLASH and TIGER MAN running over the leaves, which are
N|          somewhat BOUNCY like a huge trampoline. It's quite enjoyable.
N|          FLASH laughs aloud at the sensation, takes a big jump off
N|          the edge of one leaf, BOUNCES HIGH from the next.
O|                         
N|          Amazingly, a fat TENDRIL seizes him in mid-air, coils around
N|          his waist. FLASH yells as he is lifted further up.
O|                         
N|          AN ENORMOUS FLOWER
O|           51.
O|                         
N|          is right above him. The closed petals open. The inside is
N|          viscous, hideous looking. In the deepest recess is a dark
N|          red blob which PULSES like a huge heart, emits a BEING SOUND.
N|          With horror, FLASH realizes the tendril is feeding him into
N|          the flower's maw.
O|                         
N|          PLASH struggles vainly against the tendril's strength. TIGER
N|          MAN dashes to his rescue below, but another tendril knocks
N|          him flat.
O|                         
S|          INT. FLOWER
M|          (BARIN, FLASH)
O|                         
N|          FLASH is conveyed INTO the flower. He punches wildly with
N|          his fists, kicks, but petals are CLOSING inexorably around
N|          him. On their inner surface are deadly spiny SPIKES.
N|          Scattered around are the crushed SKELETONS of luckless TREE
N|          MEN who have been fed in here.
O|                         
N|          SWISH-PFFFFST! Out of nowhere a GLASS ARROW comes flying
N|          past FLASH'S ear, sinks itself into the flower's heart. The
N|          flower SHRIEKS. All around, FLASH, it is turning into
N|          crystalline ICE.
O|                         
N|          The tendrils lose their grip, FLASH falls onto the leaf below
N|          beside the TIGER MAN.
